{"name":"Ballet Skirt","hex":"#ffc5b3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A classical form of dance.","A theatrical presentation of such dancing, usually with music, sometimes in the form of a story."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform an action reminiscent of ballet dancing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballet"},{"term":"skirt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A separate article of clothing, usually worn by women and girls, that hangs from the waist and covers the lower torso and part of the legs.","A similar part of a dress or robe, etc., that hangs below the waist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be on or form the border of.","To move around or along the border of; to avoid the center of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skirt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballet","blocks":[{"text":"Ballet is a type of performance dance that originated during the Italian Renaissance in the fifteenth century and later developed into a concert dance form in France and Russia. It has since become a widespread and highly technical form of dance with its own vocabulary. Ballet has been influential globally and has defined the foundational techniques which are used in many other dance genres and cultures. Various schools around the world have incorporated their own cultures. As a result, ballet has evolved in distinct ways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Edgar_Degas_-_La_Classe_de_danse.jpg/330px-Edgar_Degas_-_La_Classe_de_danse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballet","wikidata":"Q41425"},{"title":"Skirt","blocks":[{"text":"A skirt is the lower part of a dress or a separate outer garment that covers a person from the waist downwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Skirt.jpg/330px-Skirt.jpg?utm_source